w is performed; the pair are actively skating, not concluding the routine.  \n\n**Character Tracking:**  \n- **Scott\u202fMoir** remains the sole male figure in focus, progressing from a lift (mis‑attributed frame) to a series of synchronized hand‑holds, lifts, and a final dynamic pose. His posture is consistently upright, controlled, and expressive of concentration.  \n- **Tessa\u202fVirtue** is continuously partnered with SM, moving through lifts, passes, spins, and finishes in tight coordination.  \n- **Background figures** (spectators, a cameraman, officials) appear only incidentally and do not perform any of the listed actions.\n\n**Conclusion:** Across frames\u202f1120‑1170, Scott\u202fMoir does **none** of the actions A–D. The sequence captures the early‑stage choreography of the Olympic ice‑dance routine, emphasizing precise partnership, fluid motion, and focused athletic poise.', 'failed_images': []}}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Looking at the evidence I\'ve gathered, I need to focus specifically on what the men did when the short program began in Sochi. The key frame is frame_1132 which shows the text "SHORT PROGRAM - TEAM COMPETITION" and "SOCHI 2014" - this appears to be the exact moment when the short program began.\n\nFrom the VLM analysis of frames 1130-1140 and 1120-1170, Scott Moir (the male skater) did not perform any of the listed actions (clapping, winking, hugging, or bowing) at the beginning of the short program. However, I need to check if there might be other men who performed these actions at this specific moment.\n\nLet me look more closely at frame_1132 and surrounding frames to see if there are other men visible who might be performing the actions.\n\n```json\n{\n    "tool": "VLM_QUERY",\n    "frames": [\n        "frames/frame_1130.jpg",\n        "frames/frame_1131.jpg", \n        "frames/frame_1132.jpg",\n        "frames/frame_1133.jpg",\n        "frames/frame_1134.jpg",\n        "frames/frame_1135.jpg"\n    ],\n    "prompt": "Loo